From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Araceae Runtime <runtime@araceae.invalid>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:33:03 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Render application context as a replaceable world-state
 section

Application additionalContext entries are no longer appended to history as
one developer message per changed key. A world-state section renders all of
them as a single <application_context> developer message:

- any value change sends the whole message again with a replacement notice
- the message is rendered again at each window start and whenever retained
  history no longer contains it, such as after local compaction
- turns that omit application context leave the model-visible context
  unchanged
- values are no longer truncated to 1,000 tokens; turn/start and turn/steer
  reject application context that would exceed 10,000 estimated tokens once
  rendered

Untrusted additionalContext keeps its user-message behavior.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
